"Duct sizing<hr/><small>Round and rectangular air ducts, ASHRAE Handbook – Fundamentals (SI), chapter 21</small>
'<!--section:air-->
'Air temperature: 't = ? {20}'°C
'Altitude of the site: 'z = ? {1190}'m
'<!--section:duct-->
'Material, roughness in mm'ε = ? {0.09}
'Airflow: 'q = ? {500}'L/s
'Size by'P_s = ? {1}' = 'x_s = ? {1}
'Rectangular duct, one side: 'a = ? {500}'mm
'<!--section:properties-->
'<div>
#hide
'Units: q L/s; D, a, b and ε mm; V m/s; p kPa; p_v Pa; Δp_L Pa/m; ρ kg/m³; μ Pa·s
'Air: standard atmosphere and ideal gas (dry air); viscosity by Sutherland
p = 101.325*(1 - 2.25577*10^-5*z)^5.2559
ρ = 1000*p/(287.055*(t + 273.15))
μ = 1.458*10^-6*(t + 273.15)^1.5/(t + 273.15 + 110.4)
c_p = 1.006
'Colebrook friction factor for Reynolds number R and relative roughness r
f_C(R; r) = $Root{1/sqr(φ) + 2*log(r/3.7 + 2.51/(R*sqr(φ))) = 0 @ φ = 0.004 : 0.2}
'Round duct of diameter d at the airflow q: velocity, Reynolds number, friction loss
V_d(d) = 4000*q/(π*d^2)
Re_d(d) = 4*ρ*q/(π*d*μ)
Δp_d(d) = 1000*f_C(Re_d(d); ε/d)/d*ρ*V_d(d)^2/2
'Equivalent diameter of a rectangular duct a × b (Huebscher)
D_eq(a; b) = 1.3*(a*b)^0.625/(a + b)^0.25
'Input error: 0 none; 1 no way of sizing chosen; 2 a value that is not above 0
n_err = 0
#if or(or(P_s < 1; P_s > 3); P_s ≠ round(P_s))
 n_err = 1
#else if or(or(q ≤ 0; x_s ≤ 0); or(a ≤ 0; ε < 0))
 n_err = 2
#end if
#if n_err ≡ 0
 'The round duct: sized by friction rate or by velocity, or given
 #if P_s ≡ 1
  Δp_L = x_s
  D = $Root{Δp_d(d) = Δp_L @ d = 10 : 10000}
 #else if P_s ≡ 2
  V = x_s
  D = sqrt(4000*q/(π*V))
 #else
  D = x_s
 #end if
 f = f_C(Re_d(D); ε/D)
 'The rectangular duct: side b for the same friction, rounded up to 25 mm, and its friction loss
 b_0 = $Root{D_eq(a; β) = D @ β = 1 : 100*D}
 b = 25*ceiling(b_0/25)
 D_e = D_eq(a; b)
 Δp_L,r = Δp_d(D_e)
#end if
'Shown: formula = result. #round keeps the constants of each line exact; some results have a format
'of their own (:0.##). A format stays with its variable as a unit, which functions refuse: only
'results that no function uses later are formatted.
#show
#nosub
#if n_err ≡ 0
 #round 6
 '<p>Atmospheric pressure, standard atmosphere: 'p = 101.325*(1 - 2.25577*10^-5*z)^5.2559:0.##'kPa</p>
 '<p>Density: 'ρ = 1000*p/(287.055*(t + 273.15)):0.###'kg/m³</p>
 '<p>Dynamic viscosity (Sutherland): 'μ = 1.458*10^-6*(t + 273.15)^1.5/(t + 273.15 + 110.4):0.000E+0'Pa·s</p>
 '<p>Sensible heat factor: 'ρc_p = ρ*c_p:0.##'W/(L/s·K), with 'c_p'kJ/(kg·K)</p>
#else if n_err ≡ 1
 '<p style="color:#C00000;background-color:#FFEEEE">Choose how to size the duct from the list.</p>
#else
 '<p style="color:#C00000;background-color:#FFEEEE">The airflow, the sizing value and the side must be above 0.</p>
#end if
#round default
#equ
'</div>
'<!--section:round-->
'<div>
#nosub
#if n_err ≡ 0
 #if P_s ≡ 1
  #round 1
  '<p>Diameter for this friction rate (Darcy–Weisbach and Colebrook, iterated): 'D'mm</p>
 #else if P_s ≡ 2
  #round 1
  '<p>Diameter for this velocity: 'D = sqrt(4000*q/(π*V))'mm</p>
 #end if
 #round 2
 '<p>Area: 'A = π*D^2/(4*10^6)'m²</p>
 #if P_s ≠ 2
  #round 3
  '<p>Velocity: 'V = q/(1000*A)'m/s</p>
 #end if
 #round 2
 '<p>Velocity pressure: 'p_v = ρ*V^2/2'Pa</p>
 #round 0
 '<p>Reynolds number: 'Re = ρ*V*D/(1000*μ)'</p>
 #round 3
 '<p>Friction factor (Colebrook): 'f:0.####': '1/sqr(f)' and '-2*log(ε/(3.7*D) + 2.51/(Re*sqr(f)))'</p>
 #round 2
 '<p>Friction loss (Darcy–Weisbach): 'Δp_L = 1000*f*p_v/D'Pa/m</p>
 #if Re < 4000
  '<p style="color:#C00000;background-color:#FFEEEE">The flow is not fully turbulent (Re below 4000): Colebrook does not apply.</p>
 #end if
#else
 '<p>No size: correct the inputs.</p>
#end if
#round default
#equ
'</div>
'<!--section:rectangular-->
'<div>
#nosub
#if n_err ≡ 0
 #round 0
 '<p>Other side for the same friction (Huebscher), rounded up to 25 mm: 'b'mm</p>
 #round 3
 '<p>Equivalent diameter: 'D_e = 1.3*(a*b)^0.625/(a + b)^0.25:0.#'mm</p>
 #round 2
 '<p>Velocity: 'V_r = 1000*q/(a*b)'m/s; velocity pressure 'p_v,r = ρ*V_r^2/2'Pa</p>
 '<p>Friction loss, from the equivalent diameter: 'Δp_L,r:0.##'Pa/m</p>
#else
 '<p>No size: correct the inputs.</p>
#end if
#round default
#equ
'</div>
